explorations.core_result:
For every \(b\in\mathbb{Z}^m\) with \(b-r\in D^{i+1}\mathbb{Z}^m\), the set \(P(b)^{(i+1)}\) is represented by integer matrices \(B',C'\) and an integer vector \(f_r'\) satisfying \(\|B'\|_\infty\le n^{i+1}\Delta\). Consequently:
- \(P(b)^{(i+1)}=\{x:B'x\le f_r'+C'(b-r)/D^{i+1}\}\) with all data integer;
- the right‑hand side is integer for each such \(b\);
- the norm bound \(\|B'\|_\infty\le n^{i+1}\Delta\) holds exactly as required for the elementary‑closure hypothesis at the next inductive level.  
Thus the representation is fully compatible with repeated closure use, and the inductive step can be iterated.
